{"author":{"id":"686d9350e5e426946f54ca7a73ceeef9fd8682b44ea6617ce58187e451c43768"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790696134,"nonce":"MNVjuhsg6LbQH6Iu1ge+aeu/sFI=","title":"Exercise xgpu.wasm in a real browser","message":"The release workflow builds and links the threaded xgpu.wasm side module and checks its exports, but no browser executes it. Add a CI test that loads the release-path bundle through Ash, requests a browser adapter and device, runs an integer compute pass with exact readback, renders known pixels to a canvas or offscreen target, and observes a rejected asynchronous operation through ash.Future.\n\nThe test must use the generated gpu API and the shipped gpu-agent.mjs, gpu.mjs, and gpu-worker.mjs modules. It should fail on mailbox wiring, dylink relocation, shared-memory setup, Future wakeup, or WebGPU command errors rather than merely proving that the JavaScript parses.","files":null}]}